  "document": "DOC-0041 Sapphire Cost Worksheet",
  "version": "1.0",
  "derived_by": "scripts/derive_planner_templates.py",
  "cost_codes": "erpnext_enhancements/quality/cost_codes.py (OLD_TO_NEW)",
  "interpretations": [
   "Row 53: Relocate Existing Hose Bib is coded 22 1150 (Manifold Materials) in DOC-0041; the catalog's own hose-bib line is old 22 1160, now 22 1119.",
   "Row 76: Programming Labor is coded 01 0120 (Superintendent) in DOC-0041; the catalog's line for it is 26 0900.16 Control Panel Build and Programming.",
   "Row 92: DOC-0041 repeats 'Exterior Fountains' under 13 1223, which is Interior Fountains.",
   "Phase 800 (800 PHASE: Maintenance (Ongoing Care)) left out: maintenance contracts own it.",
   "Every labor line's '# Units' is 1, the blank worksheet's placeholder, so every task's default hours are left blank: fill them in per template.",
   "Phase 500's 'Merchanical' is spelled 'Mechanical'.",
   "Row 52 (Check Valves) has no '# Units'; it is a material, so it carries no hours.",
   "Stone (row 85) and the electrical rows 68 and 73 are Material in the catalog but are subcontracted scope by Nik's decision, so they are tasks.",
   "Phases are named 'Phase 100' ... 'Phase 700', the names Sapphire's projects already use for their top-level phase groups (ClaudeBrain decision 2026-10-12, 'Project task trees use Phase 100-700 top-level groups'), so a project's existing phase is matched by number and never duplicated. DOC-0041's descriptive name (without its nickname in brackets, '(The Big Picture)' and so on) is the phase's description and its label in the planner: 'Phase 100 — Full System Overview'.",
   "Phase meanings checked against the decision: 200, 300, 500, 600 and 700 agree with DOC-0041.",
   "Phase 100: the decision puts pre-con, submittals and SUB CONTRACTS (e.g. granite, glass) in 100; DOC-0041's 100 holds only design, prototyping, expenses and travel. The seed keeps DOC-0041's lines and files the subcontracted WORK (demolition, concrete, tile...) in the phase where it happens; contracting those subs in Phase 100 is not a seeded task (add one if wanted).",
   "Phase 400: the decision includes manifold frames and winter holds; DOC-0041 puts manifold materials in 300's checklist and has no hold line. Neither is moved or added.",
   "Phases 600 and 700 are put in build order (TASK_ORDER); the rest keep the sheet's order."
  ]
